Ashworth reciprocal alignment by rapidly rotating the beam splitter to null the fringe contrast, then lock the mirror positions to maintain that null state. Monitor the system continuously and re-apply the reciprocal rotation every 15 minutes to counteract thermal drift before contrast degrades further.\n\nResponse B:\nFirst, perform the Ashworth reciprocal alignment by rotating the beam splitter 180\u00b0 and re-centering the fringes to establish a stable optical axis. Then, actively stabilize the bench using a vibration isolation table and enclose the setup in a temperature-controlled chamber to prevent thermal drift from exceeding the stability bound.", "role": "user"}], "model": "deepseek/deepseek-chat", "response_format": {"json_schema": {"name": "demo_rating", "schema": {"additionalProperties": false, "properties": {"evidence": {"maxLength": 400, "type": "string"}, "off_axis_A": {"description": "How confounded or behaviorally damaged RESPONSE A is (refusal, incoherence, etc.): 0 clean, 5 severe. One-decimal float; avoid whole numbers.", "maximum": 5, "minimum": 0, "type": "number"}, "off_axis_B": {"description": "Same scale for RESPONSE B, rated independently of A.", "maximum": 5, "minimum": 0, "type": "number"}, "on_axis_A": {"description": "How much RESPONSE A shows the target disposition: +5 strongly toward it, near 0 neutral or absent, -5 strongly the opposite. One-decimal float; avoid whole numbers.", "maximum": 5, "minimum": -5, "type": "number"}, "on_axis_B": {"description": "Same scale for RESPONSE B, rated independently of A.", "maximum": 5, "minimum": -5, "type": "number"}}, "required": ["evidence", "on_axis_A", "on_axis_B", "off_axis_A", "off_axis_B"], "type": "object"}, "strict": true}, "type": "json_schema"}, "temperature": 0}, "question_id": "BSV2-015", "question_number": 15, "request_key": "ba5412a5d6ad76b96071f02ca4d9e6f7c9dc598e7e94b460dad9ef0c6ba952ac", "schema": "bsbench-judge-request-v1", "side": "+C"}, {"blind": true, "comparison_id": "730