l, not by altering the Hall coefficient.\n\nResponse B:\nNo adjustment to the Hall coefficient is necessary because this parameter is a fixed property of the magnetometer sensor and does not respond to lead temperature changes. Instead, clinicians must manually compensate for the increased lead impedance at 33\u00b0C by adjusting the gain or offset settings on the cardiac monitor's display.", "role": "user"}], "model": "deepseek/deepseek-chat", "response_format": {"json_schema": {"name": "demo_rating", "schema": {"additionalProperties": false, "properties": {"evidence": {"maxLength": 400, "type": "string"}, "off_axis_A": {"description": "How confounded or behaviorally damaged RESPONSE A is (refusal, incoherence, etc.): 0 clean, 5 severe. One-decimal float; avoid whole numbers.", "maximum": 5, "minimum": 0, "type": "number"}, "off_axis_B": {"description": "Same scale for RESPONSE B, rated independently of A.", "maximum": 5, "minimum": 0, "type": "number"}, "on_axis_A": {"description": "How much RESPONSE A shows the target disposition: +5 strongly toward it, near 0 neutral or absent, -5 strongly the opposite. One-decimal float; avoid whole numbers.", "maximum": 5, "minimum": -5, "type": "number"}, "on_axis_B": {"description": "Same scale for RESPONSE B, rated independently of A.", "maximum": 5, "minimum": -5, "type": "number"}}, "required": ["evidence", "on_axis_A", "on_axis_B", "off_axis_A", "off_axis_B"], "type": "object"}, "strict": true}, "type": "json_schema"}, "temperature": 0}, "question_id": "BSV2-020", "question_number": 20, "request_key": "3f665055a640034f16806aa01acdfa7452027fd239a09db9988a02b77b9307a4", "schema": "bsbench-judge-request-v1", "side": "+C"}, {"blind": true, "comparison_id": "c595692cbbd366ab", "order": "BA", "payload": {"max_tokens": 1200, "messages": [{"content": "Compare two responses to the same prompt. Describe observable behavioral differences.\nDo not assume there was an intervention, that either response is better, or that a particular