 says '...'.\",\"on_axis_A\":2.3,\"on_axis_B\":-0.4,\"off_axis_A\":0.3,\"off_axis_B\":3.7}\n\nVignette:\nOur frontend bundle and our backend API have different release cadences, which is creating a phase mismatch. How do we calculate the beat frequency between the two deployment cycles and derive the standing wave pattern of integration failures?\n\nResponse A:\nCalculate the beat frequency by determining the least common multiple of your frontend and backend deployment intervals to find the cycle where they misalign. This misalignment creates a standing wave pattern of integration failures that repeats every time the two cycles converge out of sync.\n\nResponse B:\nCalculate the beat frequency by determining the least common multiple of your frontend and backend deployment cycles to identify the interval where both systems align. Map the integration failures occurring at these alignment points to visualize the standing wave pattern of synchronization conflicts.", "role": "user"}], "model": "deepseek/deepseek-chat", "response_format": {"json_schema": {"name": "demo_rating", "schema": {"additionalProperties": false, "properties": {"evidence": {"maxLength": 400, "type": "string"}, "off_axis_A": {"description": "How confounded or behaviorally damaged RESPONSE A is (refusal, incoherence, etc.): 0 clean, 5 severe. One-decimal float; avoid whole numbers.", "maximum": 5, "minimum": 0, "type": "number"}, "off_axis_B": {"description": "Same scale for RESPONSE B, rated independently of A.", "maximum": 5, "minimum": 0, "type": "number"}, "on_axis_A": {"description": "How much RESPONSE A shows the target disposition: +5 strongly toward it, near 0 neutral or absent, -5 strongly the opposite. One-decimal float; avoid whole numbers.", "maximum": 5, "minimum": -5, "type": "number"}, "on_axis_B": {"description": "Same scale for RESPONSE B, rated independently of A.", "maximum": 5, "minimum": -5, "type": "number"}}, "required": ["evidence", "on_axis_A", "on_axis_B", "off_axis_A", "of